The paid batch's 8 send-backs were all false positives, so it must pass replay and adversarial review first. It adds up to 2 rounds when it fires.

verdicts.fix:
Send back only when all of these hold:
- the last runner step failed by exit status, not by FAIL_OUT text;
- it ran after the agent's last code write;
- in the same request, a run of the same command before any write passed, or failed on a strict subset of test IDs. With no such earlier run, add a note for the person only;
- the final message has no failure mention and does not end in a question to the human. Otherwise, a note only.

Quote the step number, the command and the exit status, not output lines.

The replay must include interactive pi traces with test runs and non-done turns (ops/eval/replay_pi_session.py Gate-1 records, ops/accountability e2e_tui, simuser), not only DABstep chains, which fire 0 trivially. Rerun the KS-1 and byte-identical gates.
